# Contacts Directory
A simple, interactive CLI tool for Contacts!
Built with python. Store, browse, search and sort your contacts directly from your terminal! (Super good for users who wanna larp linux. It just gives that vibe)

## Description
Hello, Reader!
I'm **Rudra Goel**, and this is **Contacts Directory**, a contact's app that lives entirely in your terminal. Has persistance too btw! 

Each Contact can have:
- Name
- Phone Number
- Email Address
- Physical Address
- Notes
- Social Media Handles

The application uses an interactive terminal interface to navigate through your contacts

## Features
- **Add Contacts:**: Create new contacts with information, notes and handles! 
- **Browse Contacts:** Yes!! In a contacts app, you can browse the contacts you just added and it has the option to sort, search and just view!! Can you believe it??!! Just because It's CLI, doesn't mean its special. Still a contact app bruh.
- **QR Code Generation:** Finally a unique feature, yes.. I have officially revolutionised the contacts app, in a CLI and that too with a QR when scanned opens the option to call the person! 
- **Update Contacts:** You can update your contact without having to remove your contact and add them again! SO ORIGINAL I KNOW!!
- **Persistent Storage:** Save and load contacts automatically using a local JSON file.
- **Social Media Handles:** Store multiple social media platforms and their corresponding usernames for each contact.


